.TH SIG_BLOCKSET 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
sig_blockset \- Block a set of signals

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/sig.h>

.IB int
.IB sig_blockset(const void* set);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBsig_blockset\fR function blocks a set of signals. It takes one argument: a set of signals to block. The function returns 0 on success, -1 on failure.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB set
The set of signals to block.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 0 on success, -1 on failure.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBsig_blockset\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/sig.h>

int main() {
    sigset_t set;
    sigemptyset(&set);
    sigaddset(&set, SIGINT);
    sigaddset(&set, SIGTERM);

    printf("Blocking signals...\n");

    int r = sig_blockset(&set);

    if(r == 0)
        printf("Signals blocked successfully.\n");
    else
        printf("Failed to block signals.\n");

    return 0;
}
.nef